speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, I rise on a point of order concerning a report tabled in the House today. I am referring to the third report of the Special Joint Committee on Public Service Employer-Employee Relations. I wish to point out a substantial discrepancy in the translation. On page 5 of the French text, paragraph (a) reads as follows:
(a) Les fonctions et pouvoirs du tribunal d'arbitrage, de l'arbitre en chef et des arbitres devraient etre confies a la Commission des relations de travail dans la Fonction publique et revoques par les membres de la Commission, siegeant en comites ou a titre personnel;
I point out to the House that that was not what the committee had in mind when it drafted that provision. The English text is the one that reflects better the opinion of the committee, and I quote from page 5 (a):

(a) The functions and powers of the Arbitration Tribunal, the Chief Adjudicator and adjudicators should be assigned to the Public Service Staff Relations Board and discharged by members of the Board, sitting as panels or as individuals;
